## Duke Dennis — 69/100, PROMISING, CREATE (revised down from 74)

A packet already existed from earlier today. Re-auditing found four things that moved it — three of them corrections to the prior packet's own claims.

**The draft regressed, not the opportunity.** Revision 1 called the draft "publish-ready at 8.5." After the editor pass it was regraded **B (8.1)** — below the publish gate. Evidence dropped 8.5 → 7. So the recommendation is now *CREATE, but not today*.

**The "exactly one biography" finding was wrong.** [HotNewHipHop](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/838392-duke-dennis-youtuber-twitch-streaming-news) published a ~1,400-word dedicated profile (Sept 2024) covering South Carolina, the Army, NBA 2K, AMP — and the rizz framing. It's aggregated, not original, and didn't rank page one on the head term, but it's a real publisher occupying 9takes' exact lane. SERP weakness: 14 → 12.

**Good news, though:** it takes the *flattening* read of rizz ("mythic figure for teenage boys," echoing Rolling Stone) — the precise reading the draft argues against. The contrarian thesis now has a dated, citable incumbent to disagree with instead of vague internet consensus.

**The arrest is answerable — the prior packet was overcautious.** It told the pipeline to omit the August 2025 incident on Tobey-style legal risk. But [NBC News](https://www.nbcnews.com/pop-culture/pop-culture-news/duke-dennis-twitch-youtube-star-arrested-playing-hide-seek-texas-mall-rcna222956), [Vibe](https://www.vibe.com/news/entertainment/duke-dennis-arrested-trespassing-evading-arrest-1235092640/), and [Spectrum News](https://spectrumlocalnews.com/tx/south-texas-el-paso/news/2025/08/04/popular-amp-streamer-duke-dennis-arrested-in-san-antonio) all covered it: booked Aug 3, 2025, Shops at Rivercenter, criminal trespassing and evading arrest, Kai Cenat present and not arrested, no conviction reported. It can be stated precisely, as charges only. Biography intent: 12 → 13.

**Source depth took the real hit: 14 → 11.** I searched specifically for a collaborator or AMP member on the record about Duke and found **none**. Every named third-party source is a ranking, event coverage, a roster listing, or aggregation — no testimony. That independently confirms the regrade's complaint that the thesis rests on two videos of him narrating himself, one a "heavily garbled" auto-transcript carrying the Army section.

**Catalyst is a better story than recorded.** He was a *student* in the 2025 inaugural class at Akron and returned as a **professor** for 2026 — roster revealed July 6, event July 15–20 at Hendrix College. The promotion arc is what the draft's "Professor Dennis's syllabus" section should stand on.

Two things I deliberately did not assert: the richer Streamer University bio language floating in search summaries is **not** on the official staff page (fetched directly — it says only "Selected to be a professor at Streamer University 2026"), and Vibe/Ebony were unfetchable (tollbit paywall, 403), so their specifics are flagged as search-summary-derived rather than quoted.

**Next step is the draft, not the research.** The six open items are listed in the packet's Content requirements — the first three come straight from the grade sidecar and are worth ~1.5 points, enough to clear the gate. No files outside the packet were touched.
